-- title:
--   ofIdealTop is multiplicative on products of ideals
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and let $I, J$ be ideals of the ring $\Gamma(X, \top) = \Gamma(X, \mathcal{O}_X)$ of global sections. For an ideal $K$ of $\Gamma(X,\top)$, `Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop K` is the ideal sheaf datum on $X$ whose component at an affine open $U \subseteq X$ is the image $K \cdot \Gamma(U,\mathcal{O}_X)$ of $K$ under the restriction homomorphism $\Gamma(X,\top) \to \Gamma(U, \mathcal{O}_X)$, and multiplication of ideal sheaf data is taken componentwise, the component of a product at $U$ being the product of the two ideals of $\Gamma(U,\mathcal{O}_X)$. The theorem asserts the equality of ideal sheaf data $$\mathrm{ofIdealTop}(I J) = \mathrm{ofIdealTop}(I)\cdot \mathrm{ofIdealTop}(J),$$ that is, for every affine open $U$ of $X$ the ideal of $\Gamma(U,\mathcal{O}_X)$ generated by the restrictions of the products $ij$ ($i \in I$, $j \in J$) coincides with the product of the ideal generated by the restrictions of $I$ and the ideal generated by the restrictions of $J$. No hypotheses beyond $X$ being a scheme are imposed; in particular no finiteness, reducedness or affineness assumption is needed.
--
--   This is the multiplicativity of the passage from ideals of global sections to quasi-coherent ideal sheaves; iterating it gives the corresponding statement for powers and finite products. It is used in the explicit resolution computations for crossing quotients of polynomial rings, where a product of powers of the ideal sheaves attached to several global sections is identified with the ideal sheaf attached to a single product of sections.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_ofIdealTop_mul.lean

